<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<SActionScript version="1" name="automation_pan_write_pass">

  <!-- Proposal 49 M4, AC4.4: A TOUCH PASS ON THE PAN KNOB IS ONE UNDO STEP,
       AND IT IS HEARD. The pan twin of `automation_write_pass`.

       The single-action property is the thing most easily got wrong: a
       recorder that submitted an action per tick would put thirty entries a
       second on the undo stack, and one Ctrl-Z would peel a 33 ms sliver off
       the pass. Here THREE ticks are reverted by ONE `undo`.

       The ticks arrive through `automation-write-tick`, which feeds the
       recorder and pushes no undo step of its own — exactly as the pan knob
       moving mid-pass does, because `SSMVMixerControl::applyPan_` and
       `SMixerStrip::applyPan_` both OFFER the value to the recorder first and
       return if it was taken. The verb REJECTS a lane that is not in
       touch/latch/write, so a case cannot pass by ticking into the void.

       THE TRANSPORT IS REAL (RUN_SERIAL, SMARAGD_CAPTURE_SPEED=1), so
       `wait-playhead` waits on an actual playhead and the ticks land during
       actual playback. The pass ends at the TRANSPORT STOP.

       ============================================================== audio

       Fixture ../test_autosaw.wav: A = 0.230956 on both (identical) channels.

       THE RECORDER WRITES **LINEAR** POINTS, not step — `SAutomationRecorder`
       uses Step for `self:Muted` alone and Linear for every other target,
       which is right for a knob being dragged. So the windows between the
       ticks are RAMPS, and each one's rms is A times the root-mean-square of
       the law over that sweep, integrated in the PAN value (49 D3):

         window        pan sweep    ch0                ch1
         [0.0, 0.5)    -1 held      0.230956           0.000000  (exactly)
         [0.5, 1.0)    -0.5 -> 0    0.230956           0.208924
         [1.0, 1.5)     0 -> +1     0.163311           0.230956
         [1.5, 2.0)    +1 held      0.000000  (exact)  0.230956

       The first window holds because the SEEDED point at 0 is `step`; the
       last holds because it is the final point.

       The EXACT zeros are what make this a gate rather than a smoke test: the
       law's far side is exactly 0.0 at |p| = 1, so `minRms="0.0"
       maxRms="0.0"` is a real assertion and not a band. And the two ramp
       figures are the ones that would move if the curve were interpolated in
       the GAIN rather than in the pan VALUE — 0.208924 is the same number
       `automation_pan_ramp` reads over its own quarter-sweep, for the same
       reason.

       NOT GATED HERE, and the M4 sabotage pass is what established it rather
       than assumed it: the knob's own OFFER-TO-THE-RECORDER-FIRST rule.
       `automation-write-tick` feeds `SAutomationRecorder` DIRECTLY, so it
       cannot see whether a real control offered its value first — deleting the
       offer from `applyPan_` leaves every assertion here green.

       A section driving the REAL slider (`mixer-strip-set control="pan"`,
       added for exactly this) was written and then REMOVED as vacuous, and the
       reason is worth recording because it is M3's doing: `set-track-pan` on a
       Read-family lane REDIRECTS to a point at the locator, so a knob that
       skipped the offer writes a point too and the STORED pan is unchanged
       either way. The only discriminator left is the number of UNDO ENTRIES
       three moves leave behind — one for a taken pass, three otherwise — and a
       case counting those has to survive `set-automation-points` coalescing
       two passes on one lane. That shape was not stabilised here; the verb is
       committed and this is named rather than implied.

       The audio is measured through a RENDER after the stop, not through the
       capture backend. The pass's own ticks are wall-clock; the CURVE it
       committed is not, and a render of that curve is deterministic. What the
       capture could add here is that the pan was audible DURING the pass,
       which is proposal 21 D2's one-reposition transient territory and is not
       what AC4.4 asks.
  -->

  <setup project="new"/>

  <actions>
    <add-track index="-1"/>
    <!-- Named up here, and the lane is created in TOUCH, so that NOTHING
         undoable sits between the two passes below: the case's whole claim is
         that each pass is exactly ONE undo entry, and a stray setup action
         between them would be peeled by an undo meant for a pass. -->
    <set-track-name trackPath="0" name="PanPass"/>
    <add-sample trackIndex="0" filePath="../test_autosaw.wav" timePos="0"/>

    <!-- The lane, in TOUCH. One point at 0 so the state the undo returns to is
         exact rather than "no lane". -->
    <add-automation-lane owner="0" target="self:Pan" mode="touch">
      <p t="0" v="-1" c="step"/>
    </add-automation-lane>
    <assert-automation-value owner="0" target="self:Pan"
                             time="0" value="-1" tolerance="1e-9"
                             mode="touch" pointCount="1"/>

    <!-- Before: the lane holds -1 at all three tick positions. These are the
         assertions the undo at the end has to restore. -->
    <assert-automation-value owner="0" target="self:Pan"
                             time="24000" value="-1" tolerance="1e-9"/>
    <assert-automation-value owner="0" target="self:Pan"
                             time="48000" value="-1" tolerance="1e-9"/>
    <assert-automation-value owner="0" target="self:Pan"
                             time="72000" value="-1" tolerance="1e-9"/>

    <!-- ==================== THE PASS ====================
         `time` is given explicitly so the POINTS are exact while the transport
         is genuinely running; a tick taking the live locator instead would
         make every number above a measurement of this machine's scheduling. -->
    <set-locator position="0"/>
    <toggle-playback play="1"/>

    <wait-playhead position="24000" minAdvance="4096" timeoutMs="20000"/>
    <automation-write-tick owner="0" target="self:Pan"
                           time="24000" value="-0.5"/>

    <wait-playhead position="48000" minAdvance="4096" timeoutMs="20000"/>
    <automation-write-tick owner="0" target="self:Pan"
                           time="48000" value="0"/>

    <wait-playhead position="72000" minAdvance="4096" timeoutMs="20000"/>
    <automation-write-tick owner="0" target="self:Pan"
                           time="72000" value="1"/>

    <wait-playhead position="96000" minAdvance="4096" timeoutMs="20000"/>
    <toggle-playback play="0"/>

    <!-- The stop committed the pass: all three ticks are on the lane, plus the
         point that was already there. -->
    <assert-automation-value owner="0" target="self:Pan"
                             time="24000" value="-0.5" tolerance="1e-9"
                             pointCount="4"/>
    <assert-automation-value owner="0" target="self:Pan"
                             time="48000" value="0" tolerance="1e-9"/>
    <assert-automation-value owner="0" target="self:Pan"
                             time="72000" value="1" tolerance="1e-9"/>

    <!-- ==================== IT IS HEARD ==================== -->
    <render filename="apwp.wav" format="wav" quality="10" durationSec="2.0"/>
    <assert-audio-energy filename="apwp.wav" channel="0"
                         startFrame="0" frameCount="24000"
                         minRms="0.2287" maxRms="0.2333"/>
    <assert-audio-energy filename="apwp.wav" channel="1"
                         startFrame="0" frameCount="24000"
                         minRms="0.0" maxRms="0.0"/>
    <assert-audio-energy filename="apwp.wav" channel="0"
                         startFrame="24000" frameCount="24000"
                         minRms="0.2287" maxRms="0.2333"/>
    <assert-audio-energy filename="apwp.wav" channel="1"
                         startFrame="24000" frameCount="24000"
                         minRms="0.2068" maxRms="0.2111"/>
    <assert-audio-energy filename="apwp.wav" channel="0"
                         startFrame="48000" frameCount="24000"
                         minRms="0.1617" maxRms="0.1650"/>
    <assert-audio-energy filename="apwp.wav" channel="1"
                         startFrame="48000" frameCount="24000"
                         minRms="0.2287" maxRms="0.2333"/>
    <assert-audio-energy filename="apwp.wav" channel="0"
                         startFrame="72000" frameCount="24000"
                         minRms="0.0" maxRms="0.0"/>
    <assert-audio-energy filename="apwp.wav" channel="1"
                         startFrame="72000" frameCount="24000"
                         minRms="0.2287" maxRms="0.2333"/>

    <!-- ============ ONE UNDO REVERSES THE WHOLE PASS ============ -->
    <undo count="1"/>
    <assert-automation-value owner="0" target="self:Pan"
                             time="24000" value="-1" tolerance="1e-9"
                             pointCount="1"/>
    <assert-automation-value owner="0" target="self:Pan"
                             time="48000" value="-1" tolerance="1e-9"/>
    <assert-automation-value owner="0" target="self:Pan"
                             time="72000" value="-1" tolerance="1e-9"/>
  </actions>

</SActionScript>
